---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy — GeoScore">
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <div class="text-center mb-10">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-brand-500/10 text-brand-400 border border-brand-500/20 mb-4">
        Legal
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400">Last updated: 2026-11-01</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card p-8 space-y-6 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">1. Overview</h2>
        <p>
          GeoScore is an open-source GEO audit tool with free single-browser audits and optional Pro monitoring. This policy explains what data each mode collects and why.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The two modes handle your data differently. A <strong>free audit runs in your browser</strong>. <strong>Pro monitoring is server-side</strong>: the site you add is audited on a weekly schedule from our servers, and the results — including the site URL — are stored in our database so we can show you history, alerts and PDF exports.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">2. The URL You Audit</h2>
        <p>A free audit runs in your browser. When you enter a URL:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 mt-2">
          <li>It is fetched directly from your browser to the target site. When the target blocks direct browser requests, it goes through GeoScore's own proxy at geo-score-proxy.pages.dev — <strong>never through a third-party CORS proxy</strong>.</li>
          <li>It is not logged on our servers, and we keep no audit history for anonymous visitors. Your audit history stays in your own browser's local storage.</li>
          <li><strong>The bare hostname is sent to Google Analytics</strong> as an event property (for example <code class="text-gray-400 bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">example.com</code> — never the path or query string), so we can see which domains get audited. It is not sent to any advertising network.</li>
          <li>If you use the optional "help me fix it" form, the URL you entered and your email address are stored in our database so we can reply. That is the only case in which we store a URL from a free audit.</li>
          <li>If you run the <strong>AI visibility estimate</strong> (Pro, or the free check that requires signing in), we store the result: the site URL and hostname, the auto-generated question, the model's answer, and which simulated engine it was attributed to. What is sent to the model is a plain-text sample of your page — title, meta description and up to 1,200 characters of body text. These answers are produced by a language model playing each engine; they are estimates, not real engine traffic.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">3. Data We Do Collect</h2>
        <p>We use Google Analytics 4 (GA4) to understand aggregate traffic patterns. GA4 collects:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 mt-2">
          <li>Page views (URL paths only, no query strings with audit URLs)</li>
          <li>The audited hostname, as a property on audit events (hostname only, never the full URL)</li>
          <li>Referrer (the previous website you came from)</li>
          <li>Country and city (derived from IP, then discarded)</li>
          <li>Device type, browser, operating system</li>
          <li>Screen resolution and viewport size</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">IP anonymization is enabled. We do not enable Google Signals. Adsterra may use cookies or similar technologies to serve and measure ads.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">4. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          GeoScore uses no first-party cookies. GA4 may set its own cookies for visitor identification; you can opt out via your browser's Do Not Track setting, the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>, or by blocking third-party cookies in your browser. Adsterra and its partners may set third-party cookies or device identifiers to serve and measure ads.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">5. Your Cookie Choices</h2>
        <p>
          Analytics and advertising scripts are blocked until you allow them. On your first visit a panel at the bottom of the page asks which categories you accept; nothing is requested from Google Analytics or Adsterra before you make a choice.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 mt-2">
          <li><strong>Analytics</strong> — Google Analytics 4 page-view measurement.</li>
          <li><strong>Advertising</strong> — Adsterra ad slots.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Your choice is stored in your browser's local storage under the key <code class="text-gray-400 bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">geoscore-consent-v1</code>; it is not sent to us. To change or withdraw it, open <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the footer and choose "Essential only", or turn both switches off. Newly granted categories load immediately; a withdrawal stops the scripts from being requested again on your next page load (scripts already running in the current page are not unloaded). Clearing your browser storage also deletes the choice and brings the panel back.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">6. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>GeoScore relies on the following third-party services, each with their own privacy policies:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 mt-2">
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> (Pages hosting, our own CORS proxy, and the D1 database) — <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (analytics) — <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><strong>Adsterra</strong> (advertising) — <a href="https://adsterra.com/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">Adsterra Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><strong>Google Sign-In</strong> (optional OAuth login for Pro) — <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><strong>Creem</strong> (payments; acts as Merchant of Record, so it is the legal seller for paid plans) — <a href="https://www.creem.io/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">Creem Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><strong>Resend</strong> (transactional email: login codes and receipt notices) — <a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">Resend Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><strong>TokenRhythm</strong> (language model provider for the AI visibility <em>estimate</em>; when a signed-in user runs a check, the audited page's title, meta description and a text excerpt of up to about 1,200 characters, plus the generated question, are sent to its API) — <a href="https://tokenrhythm.studio/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">TokenRhythm</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">7. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          GeoScore is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect information from children. If you believe a child has provided information, please contact us so we can remove it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy occasionally. Changes will be posted on this page with a revised "Last updated" date. Material changes will be noted in the GitHub repository changelog.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">9. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions or data requests, open an issue at <a href="https://github.com/qq136692547-cmyk/geo-score/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">github.com/qq136692547-cmyk/geo-score/issues</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can also email us at <a href="mailto:qq136692547@gmail.com" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">qq136692547@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
